-- title:
--   First-order invariant representatives modulo (x) I
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative ring $B$, and let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module datum over $B$ in the sense of the project structure `FormalODModule` (a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $X.F$ together with an action of $\mathbb{Z}_p^2$ by endomorphisms of the law, a further endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi=[p]$ and $\varpi\circ a=\mathrm{Frob}(a)\circ\varpi$); only the underlying law $X.F$ occurs in the hypotheses below. Let $I$ be an ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ such that some power $q$ satisfies $x_i^{q}\in I$ for $i=1,2$, and such that for every $f\in I$ the series obtained by substituting the group law $X.F$ into $f$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x_1,x_2,y_1,y_2]\!]$ generated by the images of $I$ under the two substitutions $x_i\mapsto x_i$ and $x_i\mapsto y_i$. Let $L$ be a commutative $B$-Hopf algebra, free and finite as a $B$-module, and $\pi : B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]\to L$ a surjective $B$-algebra map with kernel $I$, such that each $\pi(x_i)$ is nilpotent, $\pi$ is given by adic evaluation (with respect to the zero ideal) at the point $(\pi(x_1),\pi(x_2))$, the comultiplication of $\pi(x_i)$ equals the $i$-th coordinate of $X.F$ evaluated at the pair of points $(\pi(x_j)\otimes 1)$ and $(1\otimes\pi(x_j))$, and the counit of $\pi(G)$ is the constant coefficient of $G$ for all $G$. Let $\delta$ be a $B$-algebra map from $S_1:=B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I^{2}$ to $S_1\otimes_B L$ which, on the class of any $G$, is the adic evaluation of $G$ at the point whose $i$-th coordinate is the $i$-th coordinate of $X.F$ evaluated at the pair $(\overline{x_j}\otimes 1)$, $(1\otimes\pi(x_j))$. Then for every $f\in I$ there exists $f'\in I$ with $f-f'\in (x_1,x_2)\cdot I$ and $\delta(\overline{f'})=\overline{f'}\otimes 1$ in $S_1\otimes_B L$.
--
--   This is the first-order step in the generation of the ideal of a finite free infinitesimal subgroup scheme of a two-dimensional formal group by invariant elements: every element of the subgroup ideal agrees, modulo $(x)\,I$, with one whose class in $B[\![x]\!]/I^2$ is a coinvariant for the level-one translation coaction. It is used in the proof of [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free).
